{"id":"16e1ac3c5936268f","group":"89","path":"89/89-df-kripke-frame-props.md","title":"Kripke Frame Properties","display":"df-kripke-frame-props — Kripke Frame Properties","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-df-kripke-frame-props","aliases":["89-df-kripke-frame-props"],"display":"df-kripke-frame-props — Kripke Frame Properties","depends_on":["[[89-df-kripke-frame]]","[[89-df-reflexive-frame]]","[[89-df-transitive-frame]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-df-kripke-frame-props"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-df-kripke-frame-props</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-kripke-frame-props — Kripke Frame Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c78d4bf1505bda5c\" href=\"?note=c78d4bf1505bda5c\" title=\"89-df-kripke-frame\">89-df-kripke-frame</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2645a0212ae48293\" href=\"?note=2645a0212ae48293\" title=\"89-df-reflexive-frame\">89-df-reflexive-frame</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5c02ba5095698c09\" href=\"?note=5c02ba5095698c09\" title=\"89-df-transitive-frame\">89-df-transitive-frame</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F=(W,R)\">\\(F=(W,R)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c78d4bf1505bda5c\" href=\"?note=c78d4bf1505bda5c\" title=\"89-df-kripke-frame\">89-df-kripke-frame</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Refl}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{Refl}(F)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Trans}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{Trans}(F)\\)</span> are the predicates from\n<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"2645a0212ae48293\" href=\"?note=2645a0212ae48293\" title=\"89-df-reflexive-frame\">89-df-reflexive-frame</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5c02ba5095698c09\" href=\"?note=5c02ba5095698c09\" title=\"89-df-transitive-frame\">89-df-transitive-frame</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\\)</span> 是下述定义的一元框架性质谓词，参数为给定框架 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kripke\\text{-}frame\\text{-}props}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\\Longleftrightarrow\n(\\mathrm{Refl}(F)\\land\\mathrm{Trans}(F)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kripke\\text{-}frame\\text{-}props}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\\Longleftrightarrow\n(\\mathrm{Refl}(F)\\land\\mathrm{Trans}(F)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>自反性：每个世界可访问自己</li>\n<li>传递性：可访问关系是传递的</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{FrameProps}(F)\\)</span> 是“同时自反且传递”的合取谓词，而非把\n两个命题误作 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> 中元素组成的有序对。</li>\n<li>这些性质对应不同的模态系统</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-kripke-frame","status":"resolved","id":"c78d4bf1505bda5c","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-kripke-frame]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-reflexive-frame","status":"resolved","id":"2645a0212ae48293","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","ex